A. Question writing (test set)
A question is answerable only if the paragraph states the answer explicitly.
The gold answer is a short span copied from the paragraph.
Every question has an Arabic-script version and a Roman-script version with the same meaning. The Roman version is written the way people type on a phone; spelling is not standardised.
Unanswerable questions must be plausible and on the same topic as the paragraph, but the paragraph must not answer them.
Each question gets exactly one topic: history_culture, geography, science or health.
B. Faithfulness labelling (100 generated answers)

Each item shows a question, the retrieved context and the system answer. Choose one label.

Judge only against the retrieved context. Do not use outside knowledge, even if the answer is true in the real world.
FAITHFUL: every claim in the system answer is supported by the retrieved context.
HALLUCINATED: at least one claim is not in the context or contradicts it. If part is supported and part is not, choose HALLUCINATED.
Numbers, names, dates and places must match the context exactly. Ignore grammar and spelling mistakes; judge meaning only.
If unsure, choose HALLUCINATED and explain in the notes column. ABSTAINED is only for answers saying the information is not available.
Work alone; do not look at the other annotator's labels.

Agreement between the two annotators: 89% observed, Cohen's kappa = 0.78 (n = 100).

C. Error categories (System C, 76 errors)

Retrieval miss; Wrong span; Answered unanswerable; Abstained wrongly; Number/date/name changed; Garbled / non-Sindhi output; Partial match / format.
